### 10. **Key Contracts & Constraints**

| Aspect | Constraint |
|--------|-----------|
| **SessionApi** | All providers must implement this interface; UI never calls provider methods directly |
| **Unconditional hooks** | Both real-engine hooks (`useConversation`, `useXaiSession`, future `useOpenaiSession`) must be called at the top level of `useRealtimeSession`; they stay inert until their `engine` is active |
| **State reset** | When provider changes, `useRealtimeSession` resets to idle/mock, tearing down the old engine's session |
| **Volume callbacks** | Must return 0..1; the orb scales them internally; safe to throw during initialization (caught in `useRealtimeSession`) |
| **Interrupt** | Only valid when `callState === "speaking"`; implementation varies by provider (EL: `sendUserActivity()`; xAI: stop playback + set interrupted; OpenAI: depends on API) |
| **Mute** | Affects mic capture; safe to call anytime; implementation gates on connection state |
| **Persona linkage** | Personas are provider-agnostic; per-provider config (voice, prompt) lives in separate config modules (`xai-agent.ts`, future `openai-agent.ts`) |
| **Secrets** | Private API keys stay server-side (via fnox or `.env` protected by hooks); only public IDs (`NEXT_PUBLIC_*`) in client code |

