### 6. **xAI Integration as Reference for OpenAI**

The xAI engine shows the pattern for adding a **second real provider**:

**File:** `/Users/jessearmand/Develop/realtime-persona/lib/realtime/use-xai-session.ts`

```typescript
export interface XaiSession {
  callState: CallState;
  turns: SessionTurn[];
  caption: string;
  start: () => void;
  stop: () => void;
  interrupt: () => void;
  setMuted: (muted: boolean) => void;
  getInputVolume: () => number;
  getOutputVolume: () => number;
}

export function useXaiSession(active: boolean, persona?: Persona): XaiSession {
  // Hooks called unconditionally, but only run when `active === true`
  const [callState, setCallState] = useState<CallState>("idle");
  const [turns, setTurns] = useState<SessionTurn[]>([]);
  const [caption, setCaption] = useState("press CALL to begin");

  // Refs for WebSocket, audio context, mic stream, playback queue
  const wsRef = useRef<WebSocket | null>(null);
  const ctxRef = useRef<AudioContext | null>(null);
  const streamRef = useRef<MediaStream | null>(null);
  const playbackRef = useRef<PlaybackQueue | null>(null);
  const earlyBufRef = useRef<EarlyAudioBuffer | null>(null);  // Early audio buffering
  const streamingRef = useRef(false);  // Streaming mode flag (after session.updated)

  const start = useCallback(() => {
    // 1. Bring up audio + mic capture IMMEDIATELY (parallel init)
    // 2. Mint ephemeral client-secret server-side at /api/xai/token
    // 3. Open WebSocket to wss://api.x.ai/v1/realtime
    // 4. On session.updated: configure + flush early audio + prompt greeting
  }, [send, teardown]);

  const stop = useCallback(() => {
    endedRef.current = true;
    teardown();
    setCallState("ended");
  }, [teardown]);

  const interrupt = useCallback(() => {
    if (stateRef.current !== "speaking") return;
    playbackRef.current?.stop();
    setCallState("interrupted");
  }, []);

  return {
    callState, turns, caption,
    start, stop, interrupt,
    setMuted, getInputVolume, getOutputVolume,
  };
}
```

**Key architectural decisions:**
- **Parallel initialization:** mic + audio context start immediately (don't wait for WebSocket)
- **Early audio buffering:** capture user speech before session is configured (`earlyBufRef`)
- **Server VAD barge-in:** `input_audio_buffer.speech_started` event stops playback
- **PCM16 codec:** mic → Float32 → PCM16 → base64 over WebSocket; reverse for playback
- **Per-persona config:** `resolveXaiAgent(personaId)` returns voice, instructions, turn-detection settings

**Token minting** (`/Users/jessearmand/Develop/realtime-persona/app/api/xai/token/route.ts`):
```typescript
export async function POST(): Promise<Response> {
  const apiKey = process.env.XAI_API_KEY;  // Server-side only (never client-visible)
  if (!apiKey) {
    return Response.json(
      { error: "XAI_API_KEY is not set on the server (provide it via fnox)." },
      { status: 500 },
    );
  }
  const upstream = await fetch("https://api.x.ai/v1/realtime/client_secrets", {
    method: "POST",
    headers: {
      Authorization: `Bearer ${apiKey}`,
      "Content-Type": "application/json",
    },
    body: JSON.stringify({ expires_after: { seconds: 300 } }),  // 5-min TTL
  });
  return new Response(text, {
    status: 200,
    headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json", "Cache-Control": "no-store" },
  });
}
```

**WebSocket protocol (simplified):**
```json
← conversation.created / session.created
  → session.update (instructions, voice, audio format, turn_detection, tools)
← session.updated
  → input_audio_buffer.append (flushed early audio)
  → conversation.item.create (greeting prompt)
  → response.create
← response.output_audio.delta (agent speaking)
← input_audio_buffer.speech_started (user barges in)
  → (stop playback, set interrupted)
```

